--- B: writes against a regular foreign key and a native one, side by side
column-privilege writer, child insert of a present key (parent unreadable, RLS hides it) | same: allowed
column-privilege writer, child insert of an absent key | same: refused 23503
parent writer without child rights, delete a referenced parent (cascade, RLS on the child) | same: allowed
parent writer, TRUNCATE the referenced parent alone | same: refused 0A000
FORCE RLS, owner inserts a child of a present key (policy hides the parent from the owner too) | same: allowed
FORCE RLS, parent writer deletes an invisible parent (no row matches, as natively) | same: allowed
FORCE RLS, visible parent 3 deleted, cascade into an invisible child | sql_saga allowed (1 rows), native allowed (1 rows)
after the cascade | parent 3 left: sql_saga 0, native 0 | child 3 left: sql_saga 0, native 0
--- deliberate differences (README)
TRUNCATE of a parent with no referencing child row | allowed (2 rows) then sql_saga allowed, native refused 0A000
